4	 * Website Builder — customer server actions.
5	 *
6	 * EVERY export here is a public network endpoint (a `"use server"` module), so
7	 * every function calls `requireUser()` and proves ownership of the Site by
8	 * `userId` before touching it — a customer must never read, edit, publish, or
9	 * delete another customer's site. The heavy lifting (rendering + writing the
10	 * bundle to nginx) happens in the worker (worker/site-publish.ts) behind the
11	 * SITE_PUBLISH / SITE_UNPUBLISH jobs; this file only validates, persists drafts,
12	 * and enqueues.
